{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Is it fat.</b> In wealth and possessions, as it says: אֲשֶׁר לֹא בְמִסְכֵּנֻת תֹּאכַל בָּהּ לֶחֶם (Deuteronomy 8:9)." "<b>Is there a tree in it.</b> Vine and fig and pomegranate, oil-olive and honey — that in which it is praised." "<b>And you shall strengthen yourselves and take of the fruit of the land.</b> To take hold of it, and do not fear lest they set their eyes upon you as spies." "<b>And the days were the days of the first-ripe grapes.</b> And the fruits in which it is praised were not yet in their perfection; nevertheless our master Moses trusted that the size of the fruits and their taste even at that time would suffice to testify to the praise of the land and its goodness."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:38.483644855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}